WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.085 --> 00:00:05.983
There hadn't been a celebration at Dorincourt Castle for years.

2
00:00:05.984 --> 00:00:11.682
But now the earl wanted to throw a grand dinner party to show off his grandson.

3
00:00:11.683 --> 00:00:16.574
He had no idea that bad news would arrive that night.

4
00:00:16.575 --> 00:00:22.008
The earl invited all the lords and ladies he knew.

5
00:00:22.009 --> 00:00:26.059
He even invited his sister, Constantia, to visit.

6
00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:33.332
They'd quarreled 35 years ago, and he hadn't seen her since.

7
00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:37.917
Constantia arrived a few days before the party.

8
00:00:37.918 --> 00:00:41.088
The first thing she wanted was to meet Cedric.

9
00:00:41.089 --> 00:00:47.323
"I've heard the boy has worked miracles on you, John," she teased her brother.

10
00:00:47.324 --> 00:00:53.471
"Some of the tenants have even stopped calling you 'the wicked Earl of Dorincourt.'"

11
00:00:53.472 --> 00:00:58.902
The earl scowled. "I don't know about that."

12
00:00:58.903 --> 00:01:07.395
His face brightened when Cedric entered the library. "Come here, Cedric!" The

13
00:01:07.396 --> 00:01:14.304
boy ran to his grandfather, who held out a hand to a lady with white curls and friendly eyes. "I'd

14
00:01:14.305 --> 00:01:20.479
like you to meet your great-aunt, Lady Constantia." Cedric

15
00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:26.722
shook her hand. "I'm pleased to meet you, Great-Aunt Constantia." Constantia

16
00:01:26.723 --> 00:01:29.677
smiled warmly at him. "I

17
00:01:29.678 --> 00:01:35.737
was always fond of your papa, and you remind me so much of him." "It

18
00:01:35.738 --> 00:01:41.667
makes me happy when people say that, because everyone liked him," Cedric said. "Everyone

19
00:01:41.668 --> 00:01:47.771
likes my mother too. While you're here, I hope you can meet her." "I

20
00:01:47.772 --> 00:01:55.249
hope so too." Constantia raised her eyebrows at the earl, who looked away. "The

21
00:01:55.250 --> 00:02:00.680
workmen are putting a new roof on a cottage," Cedric said to his grandfather. "Do

22
00:02:00.681 --> 00:02:03.648
you want to ride over to watch?" "Another

23
00:02:03.649 --> 00:02:12.011
time," the earl said. "Wilkins will take you riding today." After

24
00:02:12.012 --> 00:02:17.765
Cedric left the library, the earl and his sister sat down for tea. "You

25
00:02:17.766 --> 00:02:25.011
couldn't have found a better heir." Constantia

26
00:02:25.012 --> 00:02:31.772
poured the tea. "You must be pleased." "He's

27
00:02:31.773 --> 00:02:35.971
a fine fellow, and we're great friends." The

28
00:02:35.972 --> 00:02:42.557
earl started to smile. "I've actually become quite fond of him." "What

29
00:02:42.558 --> 00:02:46.742
does his mother think of you?" The

30
00:02:46.743 --> 00:02:53.053
earl's smile faded into another scowl. "I haven't asked her." "I

31
00:02:53.054 --> 00:02:58.307
must be frank with you, John, and say that I don't approve of what you've done. It's

32
00:02:58.308 --> 00:03:04.620
wrong to separate the child from his mother." Constantia put down her teacup. "I

33
00:03:04.621 --> 00:03:07.298
intend to call on her tomorrow. So

34
00:03:07.299 --> 00:03:11.551
if you're going to quarrel with me, you'd better do it now." The

35
00:03:11.552 --> 00:03:16.985
earl had forgotten that his sister never hesitated to say what she thought. "From what

36
00:03:16.986 --> 00:03:24.766
I've heard," Constantia said, "she has been a wonderful influence on her son. I've also

37
00:03:24.767 --> 00:03:29.547
heard that your tenants adore her." "They adore

38
00:03:29.548 --> 00:03:34.536
him ." The earl corrected his sister. "You

39
00:03:34.537 --> 00:03:45.147
can go see her, if you like. Just don't try to make me visit her!" ***

40
00:03:45.148 --> 00:03:50.680
The next day Constantia returned from visiting Mrs. Errol.

41
00:03:50.681 --> 00:03:55.257
"She's a perfectly lovely person," Constantia told her brother.

42
00:03:55.258 --> 00:04:00.209
"You should thank her for making Cedric the fine boy that he is."

43
00:04:00.210 --> 00:04:03.226
The earl harrumphed at Constantia.

44
00:04:03.227 --> 00:04:08.648
But she noticed he didn't say anything bad about Mrs. Errol.

45
00:04:08.649 --> 00:04:15.536
*** The dinner party was that night. Cedric put on his best black velvet

46
00:04:15.537 --> 00:04:21.948
suit. Before he went downstairs to the ballroom, he stuffed Dick's handkerchief into a

47
00:04:21.949 --> 00:04:28.765
pocket. "I wish Dick could see me wearing this to a party," he said to

48
00:04:28.766 --> 00:04:33.105
himself. At the party all the guests wanted to talk to

49
00:04:33.106 --> 00:04:37.785
Cedric. They smiled when he showed them Dick's red-and-purple

50
00:04:37.786 --> 00:04:42.479
gift. They were charmed by his kindness toward the

51
00:04:42.480 --> 00:04:48.143
earl. Constantia watched as Cedric followed his grandfather around the

52
00:04:48.144 --> 00:04:53.046
ballroom. "John's own sons never paid him this much attention," she

53
00:04:53.047 --> 00:04:57.152
thought. "No wonder John enjoys his

54
00:04:57.153 --> 00:05:04.080
company." Soon a footman approached the earl. "Should I announce that dinner is served, my

55
00:05:04.081 --> 00:05:06.696
lord?" The earl looked at his watch and

56
00:05:06.697 --> 00:05:12.565
frowned. "Mr. Havisham isn't here yet. Has there been any word from

57
00:05:12.566 --> 00:05:14.705
him?" "No, my

58
00:05:14.706 --> 00:05:21.117
lord." "This is most unusual. Mr. Havisham is always on

59
00:05:21.118 --> 00:05:24.979
time." The earl checked his watch

60
00:05:24.980 --> 00:05:32.655
again. "We'll wait a few more minutes. Let me know the moment his carriage arrives."

61
00:05:32.656 --> 00:05:37.392
The footman turned and spotted the tall lawyer entering the room.

62
00:05:37.393 --> 00:05:39.982
"Mr. Havisham has arrived, my lord."

63
00:05:39.983 --> 00:05:44.666
"Yes, I can see that," the earl said impatiently.

64
00:05:44.667 --> 00:05:49.045
"Good evening, Mr. . . .," Cedric started to call out.

65
00:05:49.046 --> 00:05:57.314
"Havisham, where have you been? Why are you late?" the earl demanded. "What's wrong?"

66
00:05:57.315 --> 00:06:03.292
Mr. Havisham, who was never agitated, was pale and obviously upset.

67
00:06:03.293 --> 00:06:08.633
Before the lawyer could reply, a second footman arrived at the earl's side.

68
00:06:08.634 --> 00:06:13.135
"Cook says dinner will be ruined if it's not served immediately."

69
00:06:13.136 --> 00:06:18.796
"Then announce that dinner is served!" the earl snarled.

70
00:06:18.797 --> 00:06:22.885
"Havisham! Tell me what's wrong at once!"

71
00:06:22.886 --> 00:06:27.518
Mr. Havisham glanced around uneasily at the guests.

72
00:06:27.519 --> 00:06:34.876
"Not here. You'll want to hear the news in private."

